          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 6.6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A sports car of mass 1500 kg is moving towards the east and its velocity-time graph is shown in Fig. 6.21. Calculate the force acting on the car during"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.176,
            0.352,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) 0 s to 5 s"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.196,
            0.361,
            0.213
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) 5 s to 10 s"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.226,
            0.217,
            0.371,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) 10 s to 15 s"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.226,
            0.238,
            0.31,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.597,
            0.072,
            0.902,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "chart_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.597,
                0.072,
                0.902,
                0.242
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_chart_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "chart_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.658,
                0.244,
                0.906,
                0.274
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.21: Velocity-time graph for a sports car"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.258,
            0.406,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) During 0 s to 5 s:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.279,
            0.889,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As the velocity-time graph is a straight line inclined to the time axis, it indicates that the sports car is moving with a constant acceleration during this time interval with u = 0 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–1",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", v = 10 m "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { S } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and t = 5 s."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.332,
            0.868,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using the kinematic equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\upsilon = u + a t ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " we can find the acceleration,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.351,
            0.49,
            0.368
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–1",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " = 0 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–1",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " + (a × 5 s)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.372,
            0.352,
            0.389
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "a = 2 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.393,
            0.887,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, using the Newton’s second law of the motion F = ma, we can find the force acting on the sports car as,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.43,
            0.732,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "F = 1500 kg × 2 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " = 3000 N acting towards the east."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.451,
            0.422,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) During 5 s to 10 s:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.47,
            0.889,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As the velocity-time graph is a straight line parallel to the time axis, it indicates that the sports car is moving with a constant velocity. Hence, no force is acting on the sports car."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.523,
            0.443,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) During 10 s to 15 s:"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.543,
            0.889,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As the velocity-time graph is a straight line inclined to the time axis, it indicates that the sports car is moving with a constant acceleration in this time interval with u = 10 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–1",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", v = 0 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–1",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and t = 5 s. Using the kinematic equation v = u + at  , we can find the acceleration,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.612,
            0.493,
            0.629
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "0 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–1",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " = 10 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–1",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " + (a × 5 s)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.633,
            0.364,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "a = – 2 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.654,
            0.888,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, using the Newton’s second law of the motion F = ma  , we can find the force acting on the sports car as,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.691,
            0.557,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "F = 1500 kg × (– 2 m s"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "–2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ") = – 3000 N"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.712,
            0.888,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The negative sign shows that the force is acting in a direction opposite to the direction of motion, that is towards the west."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
